				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "JUkMyTyZDQCZxrrZDqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Getting code to execute is most likely the most tricky part of adding a language to GT. GT needs something it can hand a string of source code to, and that hands back an object it can inspect. How that something works is up to you."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "WqUFNBcrR9el0CO07z+9gQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The usual route is LanguageLink, the framework behind GT’s Python and JavaScript support. It gives you a protocol, a server runtime you can reuse, and proxies for remote objects, and for most languages it is a fine place to start. The first version of gt4carp used it, and if you want to go that way, [[The LanguageLink route]] tells you how I did it."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "jsNXmgp4QXydK539yQJ4Ng=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "We are going to take another route, though. What I really wanted was a compiler that stays alive between snippets and tells GT about types, errors, and expansions, instead of just printing results. So we are going to write a small server of our own. Don’t worry, it’s less scary than it sounds!"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-06-11T17:48:20.869905+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:45:39.487355+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "dwEUdoqdDQC+EJoFA3UANg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Both halves make a cohesive whole, so I split this chapter into sub-chapters: [[Building a server]], [[Building a client]], and [[What now?]], where we try it out."
			}
		]
